    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30977" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nĭmĭĕtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		nimius, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a too great number</i> or <i>quantity;
				a superfluity, redundancy, excess</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sanguinis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. 6, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prunarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Eutr. 10, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gaudii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 3, p. 133, 33</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Arn. 4, 133</span></i>.—In
				plur., <i><span class="en">Pall. 2, 13 <i>med.</i></span></i></div>
